            <p>
              "Cook or order in?" "One more episode or bed?" These sound silly
              to agonize over, but decision fatigue is cumulative — small loops
              add up across a day. Using the wheel for genuinely low-stakes
              choices frees up mental bandwidth for the decisions that actually
              deserve it. There is no wrong answer to "pizza or pasta," so stop
              treating the choice like there is one.
            </p>
